cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ronin: a masterless, terminal-native, provider-agnostic AI coding agent"
message: "If you use Ronin in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rohith
    family-names: Kandula
repository-code: "https://github.com/rohithkandula19/Ronin"
url: "https://github.com/rohithkandula19/Ronin"
abstract: >-
  Ronin is a Claude-Code-style AI coding agent that reads, edits, and runs code
  from the terminal, built on a provider-agnostic agent framework with evals,
  memory, security hardening, and MCP tool integrations. It runs on Claude or on
  free models (Gemini, Cerebras, Groq, OpenRouter, Ollama).
license: MIT
